   3  5  6 	1	180.0	13.5 ; warning, analog to 1	180.0	13.5
   5  6  7 	1      135.0	8.0    ; second double bond results in different angle distribution
   6  7  8 	1      150.0	6.0    ; three double bonds in a row seem to sample a broader distribution of angles with a tendency for the third doube bond to point in the opposite direction
   7  8  9 	1      135.0	8.0
   4 10 11 	1	180.0	13.5 ; warning, analog to a_ET_C1_C1_ether
  10 11 12 	1      180.0	13.5   ; can be used with CBT dihedral potential, fitted from charmm36 reference
  11 12 13 	1      180.0	13.5   ; can be used with CBT dihedral potential, fitted from charmm36 reference



;;;;;; Martini lipid topology for C18:0/22:6 LG (SDLG), generated using:
; The Martini lipid itp generator version M3.l01  Args are: -alname SDLG -alhead 'G P' -allink 'G L' -altail 'DFFDD CCCC'
; WARNING: Autogenerated and not all lipid headgroup and tail combinations have been tested;
;          used with care and see K.B. Pedersen et al. 2024 for guidance.
;
; Description:
;   A general model plasmalogen phosphatidylglycerol (LG) lipid corresponding to atomistic C18:0/22:6(4c;7c;10c;13c;16c;19c) 1-stearoyl-2-docosahexaenoyl tails.
; Parameterization:
;   This topology follows the standard Martini 3.0 lipid definitions and building block rules. 
;   Bonded parameters and mapping have been optimized as described in K.B. Pedersen et al. 2024.
; Reference(s): 
; K.B. Pedersen et al., The Martini 3 Lipidome: Expanded and Refined Parameters Improve Lipid Phase Behavior*, 
; ACS Central Science, 2025. doi: 10.1021/acscentsci.5c00755
; P.C.T. Souza et al., Martini 3: A General Purpose Force Field for Coarse-Grained Molecular Dynamics*, 
; Nature Methods, 2021. doi: 10.1038/s41592-021-01098-3
; Created: 2024.07.12
;
; Molecular topology and mapping of indices:
; GL0-PO4-GL1-D1A-D2A-D3A-D4A-D5A
;          |
;         PL2-C1B-C2B-C3B-C4B
;
;  1 - 2 - 3 - 5 - 6 - 7 - 8 - 9 
;          |
;          4 - 10- 11- 12- 13
;
;@INSANE alhead=G P, allink=G L, altail=DDDDD CCCC, alname=SDLG, charge=-1.0
;@RESNTEST SDL==SDLG if: atoms[0]==GL0
;@BEADS GL0 PO4 GL1 PL2 D1A D2A D3A D4A D5A C1B C2B C3B C4B 
;@BONDS GL0-PO4 PO4-GL1 PO4-PL2 GL1-PL2 GL1-D1A D1A-D2A D2A-D3A D3A-D4A D4A-D5A PL2-C1B C1B-C2B C2B-C3B C3B-C4B 
;

